{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.LowerBoundCannotConstrainADifference","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.LowerBoundCannotConstrainADifference","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Group.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Order.MinMax","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Abel"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.LowerBoundCannotConstrainADifference.diff_eq_of_bounds_saturated","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.LowerBoundCannotConstrainADifference.diff_eq_of_bounds_saturated","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/LowerBoundCannotConstrainADifference.lean#L109-L116","doc":"The interval of `diff_bounded_of_upper` collapses to a point exactly when\nboth bounds are tight, recovering `diff_of_saturated`. So saturation is the\n*extreme* case of the two-sided situation, not a mild simplification of it: it\nassumes the upper bound coincides with the lower one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.LowerBoundCannotConstrainADifference.diff_bounded_of_upper","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.LowerBoundCannotConstrainADifference.diff_bounded_of_upper","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/LowerBoundCannotConstrainADifference.lean#L99-L106","doc":"**What would restore a constraint without saturation: an UPPER bound.**\nGiven two-sided bounds the difference is pinned to an interval. Eq. (43) supplies\nonly the lower half, so this names the missing ingredient exactly — not more\ntopology, but an upper bound on the energy of a knotted flux configuration. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.LowerBoundCannotConstrainADifference.diff_of_saturated","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.LowerBoundCannotConstrainADifference.diff_of_saturated","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/LowerBoundCannotConstrainADifference.lean#L91-L97","doc":"**What the arc has been assuming.** If the bound is *saturated* — read as an\nequality — the difference is determined by the bounds alone. This is the step\nthat has been taken silently; here it is, with `saturation` as a named\nhypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.LowerBoundCannotConstrainADifference.no_split_value_is_excluded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.LowerBoundCannotConstrainADifference.no_split_value_is_excluded","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/LowerBoundCannotConstrainADifference.lean#L82-L88","doc":"The same fact in the form the arc needs to hear it: **no** value of the\nmirror split is excluded by the bound. Whatever the AME ladder had turned out to\nbe — constant, growing, falling, alternating — eq. (43) would have been\nconsistent with it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.LowerBoundCannotConstrainADifference.diff_unconstrained","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.LowerBoundCannotConstrainADifference.diff_unconstrained","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/LowerBoundCannotConstrainADifference.lean#L68-L80","doc":"**The result.** A lower bound on each of two quantities places *no*\nconstraint on their difference: for any target `t`, energies satisfying both\nbounds exist whose difference is exactly `t`.\n\nThe witness is explicit — push `E₂` up until `E₁ = E₂ + t` clears `B₁` as well.\nSince `E₂` may be taken arbitrarily large, `t` may be arbitrarily negative; since\n`E₁` may be, `t` may be arbitrarily positive. ","signatureChunk":0}]}